HISTORY
-------

This library is based on UCDMC99 and previous work performed at
University of California Davis, and Karl Franzens University, Graz.

It is developed and maintained at Sunnybrook and Women's
College Health Science Centre.

Contact email:
	morgan@sten.sunnybrook.utoronto.ca

Latest versions are published at:
	http://dicomlib.swresearch.ca


DEPENDENCIES
------------

The Linux/macOS C++ library build requires:

* CMake 3.16 or newer
* A C++17 compiler
* POSIX threads

Boost is no longer required. The bundled socket code is built as part of
the dicom static library.

Default implementation identity:

* Implementation Class UID: 1.2.826.0.1.3680043.10.1778
* Implementation Version Name: DICOMLIB2008


BUILD
-----

Supported targets are Linux and macOS on x86, x86_64, ARM 32-bit and ARM
64-bit processors.

	cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
	cmake --build build --parallel


REFERENCE
---------

The generated data dictionary and UID registry are based on the official
DICOM 2026c DocBook XML published by NEMA.



DOCUMENTATION
-------------

Source code is documented in a format understandable to
the DOXYGEN documentation tool.  Running the doxygen
command in the code directory will create a set of html
pages describing the code.

doxygen can be obtained from.

	http://www.doxygen.org
